16. Technical Blueprint

16.1 Proposed architecture

The recommended MVP is a modular monolith:

flowchart TD
    WEB["React Web Application"] --> API["Flask REST API"]
    API --> DB[(PostgreSQL)]
    API --> STORE["Private Object Storage"]
    API --> QUEUE["Task Queue"]
    QUEUE --> WORKER["Export and AI Worker"]
    WORKER --> STORE

This is a proposed technical baseline, not a verified deployed stack. Architecture changes should be recorded through Architecture Decision Records.

16.2 Principal modules

Identity; Catalogue; Creatives; Ready Designs; Design Sessions; Taste; Matching; Projects; Workspace; AI Orchestration; Administration; Analytics.

16.3 Core data domains

Users, client profiles, creative profiles, and roles.

Sectors, services, work examples, portfolios, and style tags.

Ready Designs, immutable versions, editable properties, licences, sessions, and exports.

Projects, services, Taste Profiles, service directions, and Creative DNA.

Recommendation runs, options, members, explanations, and feedback.

Workspace members, messages, files, milestones, feedback, approvals, and deliverables.

AI actions, rights events, audits, analytics, and operational logs.

16.4 Security and privacy baseline

Backend authorization for every protected resource.

Private object storage and short-lived authorized access.

Input, schema, upload, and file-type validation.

Secure token handling and progressive account conversion.

Rate limiting for sensitive and expensive operations.

Audit events for AI, rights, exports, handoffs, and approvals.

Data minimization and retention rules.

No secrets in source control.

No raw private project content in analytics identifiers.

